{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>ובה</b> Three times in the Masorah: here, and the others: ובה יחסו עניי עמי, ובה אבן יקרה. Meaning: ובה אדע כי עשית חסד — if she is righteous, bestowing kindnesses. ובה אבן יקרה — that he gave her silver and gold vessels and a precious stone. Thus it is in Bereshit Rabbah: Rav Huna in the name of Rabbi Yosi — אבן יקרה היתה משקלה בקע — a precious stone, its weight was a beka."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The three Masorah occurrences are all forms of ובה appearing in different contexts; the second is from 1 Samuel 22:2 and the third is the same verse being commented on here, read as an allusion to the precious stone given to Rebecca."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:47.919509195Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}